<title>GERMANY: Non-Euro nations won't abuse devaluation-Backstrom.</title>
<headline>Non-Euro nations won't abuse devaluation-Backstrom.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank governor Urban Backstrom said on Friday that nations outside the ERM 2 will not engage in competitive devaluation against the Euro.</p>
<p>&quot;I can only speak for the country I represent, but the answer is no,&quot; Urban Backstrom said when asked at the Frankfurt European Banking Congress whether nations outside the ERM 2 would consider a competitive devaluation against the Euro.</p>
<p>ERM 2 is the name given to the new exchange rate mechanism set up to include the currencies of those countries aiming to be included in Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) and the Euro single currency.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
